```js
self.addEventListener('install', event => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.open('v1').then(cache => cache.addAll(['/index.html', '/style.css']))
  );
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', event => {
  event.respondWith(
    caches.match(event.request).then(resp => resp || fetch(event.request))
  );
});
```

**Caveats**
- Requires HTTPS in production (plain HTTP won't register one, `localhost` is exempted for dev).
- The scope of the worker is limited to the directory it's served from (and below) unless you set the `Service-Worker-Allowed` header.
- Caching is easy to get wrong — bump your cache name/version on every deploy and clean up old caches in the `activate` event, or users will keep seeing stale assets indefinitely.

